      <text>2.1 HCF and LCM</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p></p><p>(a) Find the highest common factor (HCF) of {@num1@} and {@num2@}</p><p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p><p>[[feedback:prt1]]<br></p><p style="text-align: right;"><b>(2)</b></p><p><span id="docs-internal-guid-79d9d8af-7fff-614a-5ea0-3c491e790904"></span></p><p dir="ltr" style="">(b) A machine has a buzzer that sounds every {@time1@} minutes. The machine also has a bell that sounds every&nbsp;{@time2@} minutes. The buzzer and the bell sound together at {@time_init@}:\( 00 \).</p><p dir="ltr" style="">Find the time at which they next sound together, giving your answer as a 24-hour clock.</p><p dir="ltr" style="">[[input:ans2]] :&nbsp;[[input:ans3]]</p><p dir="ltr" style="">[[validation:ans2]]&nbsp;[[validation:ans3]]</p><p dir="ltr" style="">[[feedback:prt2]]<br></p><p dir="ltr" style="text-align: right; "><b>(3)</b></p><p></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
